          "Build a constituency-specific economic agenda: for the 27.4% renter population, lead with rent stabilization and tenant protections; for the 40.48% Black constituency, emphasize economic development, responsive community safety, and wealth-building in majority-Black neighborhoods; for the 25.58% Hispanic population, emphasize language access, labor rights, and immigration-responsive services.",
          "The $81,970 median household income places this district below state averages for some regions and requires an economic narrative focused on cost-of-living relief, wage growth, and public service delivery — not abstract policy debate, but concrete improvements in the lived experience of working people.",
          "Avoid ceding the 'responsive local governance' message to Republicans; the Democratic incumbent's unopposed status has created space for a challenger to position themselves as more accountable, more present, and more focused on delivering material results than an incumbent who runs without opposition."
