          { name: "Assuming Racial and Ethnic Diversity Means a Unified Minority Coalition With Identical Priorities", tag: "avoid", why: "The 41.9% Black, 38.8% white, 11.84% Hispanic, and 5.09% Asian composition, combined with 53.9% college attainment and renter concentration, describes a community where housing affordability, education investment, and economic opportunity cross racial and ethnic lines rather than organizing into separate coalitions. A candidate who campaigns to specific racial groups without understanding the shared material concerns across communities — or who assumes that demographic labels predict voting bloc behavior — will miss both the coalition-building opportunity and the material policy alignment that can hold this district durable. Housing justice, education equity, and economic opportunity benefit all communities in IL-HD-10 simultaneously." }
