          "Prioritize economic security messaging for the 54.4% Latino constituency on immigration status and workplace protections: this is a working-class community where legal status, labor law enforcement, and protection from wage theft are material economic concerns that affect household income directly. A representative who addresses these with legislative specificity—not partisan framing—commands credibility with the constituency's most economically vulnerable segments.",
          "Engage the 34.84% white minority as a genuine swing constituency: at 38.3 median age and $77,015 income, these voters are economically similar to their Latino neighbors and evaluating on identical concerns around housing costs, wage growth, and school quality. A challenger who can credibly address these shared economic concerns while rejecting racial division will find the white minority substantially more available than the unopposed result suggests.",
          "Focus campaign on specific policy delivery on housing affordability and education: with 34.5% renters and 26.4% college attainment in a district where the next generation's economic mobility depends on access to affordable housing and quality education, a legislative record that demonstrates concrete action on these material concerns will be far more persuasive than partisan loyalty or demographic representation alone."
