          "Lead with working-class economic security: at $67,530 income with 34.1% renters, the district's material concerns are housing stability, healthcare access, childcare costs, and job protection in service-sector work—not abstract party positioning; legislative record on these issues is the credibility foundation that matters most in a future competitive cycle.",
