          { name: "Assuming that Urban Affluence Means Automatic Democratic Consolidation", tag: "avoid", why: "While IL HD-42's demographic profile — high income, high education, urban location — is strongly correlated with Democratic alignment, this does not mean that the constituency is indifferent to representation quality or that it cannot be mobilized around specific grievances. The college-educated urban professional constituency is capable of registering dissatisfaction through lower turnout, strategic primary challenges, or shifts in how they evaluate candidates on specific issues. Governing as though affluent Democrats will vote Democratic regardless of performance is the fastest way to erode a 100% margin into a vulnerable 60-70% result." }
