          "Engage the Hispanic community with specific fluency on economic mobility, housing affordability, and education pipeline: the 57.78% Hispanic share and 20.8% college attainment rate mean credential pathways, skilled-trade opportunity, and first-generation homeownership are live concerns for a substantial portion of the district that deserve specific legislative attention and regular constituent contact.",
          "Defend the 64% by demonstrating competent governance on schools, public safety, and economic development: a Democratic margin this large is held by constituent perception that the incumbent is delivering, not by partisan loyalty alone — any visible governance failure on these issues will activate the 36% opposition and erode the Hispanic swing voters who form the margin's core.",
