          "Address property tax sustainability explicitly: affluent suburban households earning $124,462 are most vulnerable to property tax burden—engage directly on tax policy, reassessment reform, and the relationship between tax revenue and service delivery rather than abstract anti-tax rhetoric.",
          "Articulate a healthcare access strategy specific to high-income suburban families: these constituents have insurance but face rising deductibles, narrow provider networks, and coverage gaps; a candidate who speaks to these material concerns rather than national healthcare politics will move persuadable voters.",
          "Demonstrate fiscal competence and transparency in local governance: at this income and education level, voters evaluate incumbents and challengers on whether they manage public resources efficiently and communicate clearly about trade-offs; this is where real district-specific performance differences emerge."
