          "Avoid treating this district as safely Democratic or safely Republican; the 56-44 margin in a high-income, high-education, white-majority district is evidence that the historical basis of suburban Republican support has eroded in this specific constituency, and that erosion is reversible only through understanding and addressing the concerns that caused it.",
          "Engage the homeowner-majority constituency (83.6%) on property tax burden, school funding mechanisms, and local development governance with the specificity this affluent, educated electorate demands — generic suburban boilerplate will not persuade voters who are actively reconsidering their partisan alignment.",
