          { name: "Generic Partisan Messaging in a Constituency That Votes on Governance Competence", tag: "avoid", why: "In a district with 51.4% college education, $103,035 income, and a 59% Democratic result, voters are evaluating on substantive governance — whether local schools are improving, whether transit is functioning, whether public safety is effective, whether tax dollars are spent wisely — rather than responding to abstract partisan appeals. A campaign that relies on generic Democratic identity messaging or partisan positioning while ignoring the incumbent's specific performance on these material issues will not move votes in a constituency that values evidence-based argument and demonstrable competence; the opposition will exploit any perception that the incumbent is offering rhetoric rather than results, and in a district this educated, that argument has real purchase." }
