          "Engage the Asian and Hispanic communities with specific constituent attention rather than generic diversity messaging; at 13.28% Asian and 16.87% Hispanic in a professional-class suburb, these communities likely include business owners, healthcare professionals, and entrepreneurs whose economic concerns around business regulation, professional licensing, and tax policy are material to their vote choice.",
          "Recognize that 40% opposition in this affluent, educated district represents credible conservative voters — not fringe opposition — and any incumbent must engage their fiscal and governance concerns directly rather than dismissing them as ideologically motivated; the margin is real but contested.",
          "Build a message around public investment efficiency and outcome accountability: schools, roads, public safety, and parks are the material services that affluent suburban voters monitor closely, and demonstrating concrete results in these areas — not just budget expansion — is the foundation for holding or gaining ground in a 60-40 district."
