          { name: "Identity-Politics or Partisan Ideology Messaging", tag: "avoid", why: "IL-HD-81's college-educated, high-income, diverse (72% white, 12% Asian, 8% Hispanic, 4% Black) constituency evaluates on whether government is delivering tangible results — school quality, tax efficiency, infrastructure, public safety — not on cultural or partisan positioning. Any candidate whose messaging centers on partisan conflict, identity-group appeals, or ideological framing rather than specific accomplishments and policy plans will find that messaging actively counterproductive with voters whose education and resources give them the capacity to vote based on competence assessment rather than tribal loyalty." }
