          { name: "Dismissing Democratic Voters as Coastal Elites or Out-of-District Interests", tag: "avoid", why: "The 41% Democratic vote in IL-HD-82 is not imported from Chicago's urban core — it comes from college-educated professionals, business owners, and established suburban families who have lived in this district for decades and have real economic stakes in local governance quality. Framing this opposition as temporally transient or ideologically external rather than as a substantial and permanent part of the district's constituency will alienate independent and persuadable voters who see themselves in that 41% and respond negatively to rhetoric that treats them as interlopers in their own community." }
