          "Treat the 41% opposition as a legitimate and permanent part of the district: these are college-educated professionals and business owners, not transient voters or imported partisans. Acknowledge their concerns, respond to their specific priorities on healthcare, climate, or education, and avoid rhetoric that treats them as external to the community they live in.",
