          "Identify the ~10% demographic gap and establish baseline engagement with Hispanic, Black, and other minority constituents before an opposition campaign identifies them first as persuadable or persuaded voters.",
          "Build a legislative record on kitchen-table issues that working-class households actually face at $64,685 income in Illinois — cost-of-living pressures are the primary swing point in a district this economically positioned.",
          "Recognize that 29.1% renters in the district have materially different economic concerns than homeowners; housing policy, rental market regulations, and affordability-focused governance speak directly to a constituency that may not share homeowner priorities on property tax structure."
