          "Avoid treating unopposed status as an indicator of durable support: the absence of a 2024 challenger reflects current Democratic resource allocation, not constituent satisfaction; any incumbent who reduces constituent engagement or assumes the seat is safe risks a credible challenger emergence when Democratic resources shift to competitive suburban Illinois seats.",
          "Build a continuous constituent relationship around concrete delivery: with 20.5% college attainment and $66,722 income, IL-HD-102 voters evaluate on whether their representative has delivered measurable results on their priority issues — property tax relief, education funding, infrastructure investment — not on party affiliation or abstract messaging."
