          "Lead with specific, credible answers to affluent suburban governance concerns — property tax burden, school quality and funding, transportation infrastructure, and economic development capacity — delivered with the policy sophistication that 58.1% college education and $141,245 median income demand; generic partisan messaging will not move voters in this district.",
          "Engage the 11.45% Asian community and 9.08% Hispanic community with specificity on education policy, economic mobility, and community investment; these are swing constituencies in affluent suburbs who evaluate on policy substance and demonstrated results, not on inherited partisan loyalty or demographic assumptions.",
          "Identify and address the specific issues driving the 50% opposition — whether concentrated among property-tax-frustrated homeowners, school-quality-focused parents, or voters concerned about infrastructure investment — and offer concrete, implementable solutions rather than abstract ideological positioning."
