          "Lead with constituent service and responsive governance to affluent homeowners: at $118,948 median income and 17.8% renters, this is a property-owning constituency evaluating on school quality, infrastructure maintenance, property tax fairness, and municipal service delivery — material governance concerns where an incumbent's record can be measured and compared.",
          "Build specific relationships with Hispanic and Asian communities: the 16.5% Hispanic and 6.38% Asian populations are too large to govern around and represent the exact suburban diversity that has driven Democratic gains in Illinois suburbs — these communities require active constituent engagement, not passive assumption of Republican loyalty.",
          "Anticipate and prepare for a credible Democratic challenger: the unopposed status masks the district's inherent persuadability on suburban quality-of-life issues; any challenger who can articulate a vision of government investment in schools, infrastructure, and community services while acknowledging fiscal responsibility will have a foundation for suburban persuasion in IL-SD-33."
