          "Lead on constituent service delivery and quality-of-life issues that matter to suburban professionals: school funding adequacy, healthcare access and insurance affordability, and whether state tax policy supports or burdens working families and young homebuyers. These are the material concerns that determine whether educated suburban voters stay Republican or become available to a credible alternative.",
          "Engage the 29.6% renter population specifically on housing affordability, tenant protections, and economic mobility pathways — renters in suburban Illinois are economically precarious in ways that homeowners are not, and their needs differ from the property-owner majority. Visibility on these issues builds the constituent relationship that prevents future Democratic recruitment of this cohort.",
          "Maintain visible community presence and constituent responsiveness as the core strategic discipline — in a district where the incumbent faces no current opposition but lacks the deep partisan intensity of safely Republican rural areas, consistent engagement with constituents is the primary defense against future challenges and the condition for retaining support among college-educated and minority populations."
