          "Lead with cost-of-living and housing affordability: at $81,009 median income with 38.7% renters and a 39.2-year median age, the district's working-age households are under real financial pressure. Rent stabilization, tenant protections, wage policy, and affordable housing access are the material concerns most likely to mobilize Hispanic and Black renters and shift the current coalition.",
          "Build specific constituent service infrastructure in Hispanic neighborhoods and Black communities; unopposed elections often result in representative neglect of communities that assume they have no alternative. Active, visible service delivery and policy responsiveness in all three communities is the foundation of a durable majority.",
          "Avoid treating the unopposed victory as evidence of political strength; it is evidence of the absence of organized opposition. The demographic structure of IL-SD-39 is inherently competitive, and sustained electoral viability requires active engagement with all three major communities, not passive consolidation of a white homeowner base."
